WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.796 --> 00:00:09.700
"Here you go, Adriana."

2
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.542
Grandpa handed me an apron and a cap.

3
00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:16.624
They looked silly with red, white, and green stripes.

4
00:00:17.665 --> 00:00:18.225
I gulped.

5
00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.287
Did I really have to wear them?

6
00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.849
What if someone from school saw me?

7
00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:27.910
I didn't want to hurt Grandpa's feelings.

8
00:00:30.832 --> 00:00:34.313
He had spent the past year getting his pizzeria ready for business.

9
00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:40.896
Years ago he had been a pizzaiolo—a pizza maker—in Italy.

10
00:00:42.616 --> 00:00:47.098
Now he was finally going to make authentic Italian pizza here in America.

11
00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:49.799
His dream was coming true.

12
00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:53.060
But all I saw was a fashion nightmare.

13
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:03.602
"Pass out free slices of pizza Margherita to everyone who walks by," Grandpa instructed.

14
00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:06.422
"And be sure to tell them the story."

15
00:01:08.523 --> 00:01:13.424
I grabbed a tray and started passing out pizza slices to people from a table set up outside.

16
00:01:15.745 --> 00:01:21.506
Then I saw them: Rachel and Clara—the most popular girls at my school.

17
00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:25.067
I pulled down my cap to hide my face.

18
00:01:26.148 --> 00:01:27.408
But it was too late.

19
00:01:28.692 --> 00:01:31.034
"Hey, you're Adriana, from school, right?"

20
00:01:31.494 --> 00:01:32.255
Rachel said.

21
00:01:32.275 --> 00:01:35.637
"I didn't know there was a new pizza place in town."

22
00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:39.379
Clara was looking around.

23
00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:44.763
"Don't you have pepperoni or Hawaiian pizza?"

24
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:47.205
"Oh! Hi!"

25
00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:48.506
I blurted out.

26
00:01:50.007 --> 00:01:53.369
I lifted my cap and started talking—much too fast.

27
00:01:53.389 --> 00:01:56.251
"Yes, my grandpa owns this place.

28
00:01:56.551 --> 00:01:57.532
Today's our grand opening.

29
00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:02.806
We don't serve American-style pizza, like pepperoni or Hawaiian.

30
00:02:03.706 --> 00:02:05.688
We only have pizza like they do in Italy.

31
00:02:06.428 --> 00:02:07.869
My grandpa wants it to be authentic."

32
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.151
"Awesome," Rachel said.

33
00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:11.972
"Can we try some?"

34
00:02:11.992 --> 00:02:15.194
"Sure." I tried to act cool.

35
00:02:17.055 --> 00:02:19.937
I put two slices on plates and gave them to the girls.

36
00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:27.642
Delicious!" Clara said.

37
00:02:28.903 --> 00:02:29.624
Rachel nodded.

38
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.541
"Much better than pepperoni pizza!

39
00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:34.822
What is this called?"

40
00:02:34.842 --> 00:02:37.763
"It's called pizza Margherita.

41
00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:41.486
It was named after Queen Margherita.

42
00:02:43.026 --> 00:02:48.509
Back in 1889 in Italy, pizza was eaten mostly by workers who needed a quick lunch.

43
00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.571
But the queen was tired of fancy food.

44
00:02:52.552 --> 00:02:54.973
So she asked a pizza maker to make some pizzas.

45
00:02:56.494 --> 00:03:02.141
He made one with tomatoes, mozzarella cheese, and basil—the colors of the Italian flag!

46
00:03:03.161 --> 00:03:07.102
The queen loved it, and the pizza maker named the pizza after her.

47
00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:11.984
Soon everybody in Italy started eating pizza."

48
00:03:14.524 --> 00:03:15.225
Rachel grinned.

49
00:03:15.245 --> 00:03:18.526
"We owe a big thanks to that Italian queen!"

50
00:03:19.386 --> 00:03:21.927
"Can we try some other types of pizza?"

51
00:03:22.247 --> 00:03:22.987
Clara asked.

52
00:03:24.247 --> 00:03:26.068
I got some more slices from the kitchen.

53
00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.361
"This is pizza bianca," I said.

54
00:03:33.381 --> 00:03:35.062
"It's from Rome.

55
00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:37.503
There's no cheese—just olive oil and salt."

56
00:03:39.804 --> 00:03:44.466
Next the girls tried the Sicilian-style pizza with anchovies—and they liked that too!

57
00:03:44.486 --> 00:03:50.488
"My family is Italian American too," Rachel said.

58
00:03:50.508 --> 00:03:53.330
"But no one is good at cooking.

59
00:03:56.171 --> 00:03:58.912
You're so lucky your grandpa makes such great food."

60
00:04:00.604 --> 00:04:01.305
I smiled.

61
00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:08.050
I felt proud of my family's culture—and Grandpa.

62
00:04:09.251 --> 00:04:13.354
When the girls left, I went back inside to get more of Grandpa's delicious pizza.

63
00:04:15.615 --> 00:04:19.058
And I didn't even care about the apron or the cap anymore.
